  "notes": [
    "**Ir** is completely irregular in all tenses",
    "Preterite forms are identical to **ser** (fui, fuiste, fue, fuimos, fueron)",
    "Context determines meaning: *Fui al parque* (I went) vs *Fui estudiante* (I was)",
    "Imperfect has a unique pattern with the stem \"ib-\"",
    "Past participle: **ido** (gone)",
    "Future: regular endings attached to stem \"ir-\"",
    "Condicional: regular conditional endings attached to stem \"ir-\"",
    "Often used with \"a\" + infinitive to express near future: *Voy a estudiar* (I'm going to study)",
    "Common usage: *ir de compras* (to go shopping), *ir a pie* (to go on foot)",
    "Opposite: **venir** (to come)"
  ],
